Z||000000||TalShino||04-13-2000||03:47 PM||||General oil questions....<P>1. I know I should know this, but how much oil does my 88 2.5l hold?<P>2. I like to run my car hard, sometimes too hard, whats the best type of oil&filter I should use?<P>3. whats up with coffee cans on hondas?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||04-13-2000||09:05 PM||||1. 4 quarts, a touch more maybe with a long filter.<BR>2. there is a short and a long filter. Most of use prefer the long ones. ACDelco long is PF52, short is PF47. Filters that use Fram numbering will have 1-3 letters followed by 3980.<P>The long filter already excedes GM specifications. (GM specifies the short PF47) So pick whatever one you like, but not the cheapy store brands.<P>I've been running Quacker State Extended Protection. I'm the cheap guy at the all you can eat. I used tha case up tho so maybe I'll move to synth or a synth blend now that I fixed the leak.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||04-13-2000||10:10 PM||||Ogre, are you absolutely sure about that?  I think you're giving TalShino the info for the 84-87 Duke.  The 88 uses the in-pan filter, and to the best of my knowledge there's only one size that fits - I think it's AC #PF1072.<P>I usually use the Deutsch brand filter (from AutoZone) in my 88 Coupe - it seems to have more folded filter material than the standard AC filter.  I also use good old Valvoline dino oil, though lots of bright people swear by synthetics.<P>Also, my 88 seems to hold 4.5 qts, though all the documentation claims 4 qts.<P>As for coffee cans, your guess is as good as mine.  Too much Limp Bizkit, I guess.||||reg||1
